Sval: a private window's print job is named for the browser

nsPrintJob names a print job after the page's title, or its address when
the page has none, and the system's print queue and its job history keep
that name. A job from a private document is named with the brand's short
name. The title and address in the page's headers and footers are the
user's choice in the print dialog and are unchanged.

